Subject: [PATCH] Deaths named for what did them (queue #414, note 682)

The Householder, the Lodger, the Hanger, the Hollow House, the Brakeman, the Hot Box, Tower Jaw, the Grumbler and the Pickers each kill with a death cause of their own (appended to DeathCause), with a death-screen line and the clerk's: they had borrowed the Choir's (the director, 13 Oct: "householder grabbed me and it said seized by the choir"), the hounds', the Passenger's, a dropped load's and the Gnawers'. GDD D.12 and F.5 first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XV59m2qzBTRyKw3EDXquHM
